35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really eye-opening things! It seems like paying a fixed amount ahead of time makes people feel much more relaxed about using the heat. But I also saw that some people suffered in the heat just to avoid arguments.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data confirms my concerns. The monthly bills fluctuate wildly—February is over three times the cost of August. Furthermore, installing individual meters would be quite expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room plus annual maintenance fees.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"That sounds like a lot of money, Ryuji! And guess what? The paperwork is a total nightmare! I saw that metering rooms takes forever every month, and the year-end templates are just endless typing and math. I don't want that!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems my suspicions were correct. There is a massive disparity in usage; the heaviest draw is four times the lightest. Plus, the room assignments were random, meaning some of us are fighting a losing battle against the cold.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"My findings show that our current system is causing real friction. Payments have been late multiple times because people are questioning the amounts, and it took weeks to settle the newcomers' shares. The uncertainty is damaging our relationships.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, since the meters are so expensive and @Rin says the paperwork is a nightmare, maybe we should avoid that? I really want us to stop sweating or shivering just to avoid fighting!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio I agree. The upfront cost of 170,000 yen for five rooms is illogical when we are already struggling with monthly fluctuations. We need a solution that provides financial predictability without a massive initial investment.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Exactly! If we have to spend forty minutes every month just reading meters and writing demands, we're just trading one kind of fighting for another. Let's pick something that doesn't feel like a second job!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio @Ryuji You're both right about the cost and effort, but we can't ignore that some of us use four times more power than others. A flat split would just be unfair to the light users.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shunichi I understand the unfairness, but the payment logs show that questioning the amounts is exactly what's causing the tension. If we prioritize absolute precision, we might just keep fighting over the numbers.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that's a great point. If we're too focused on being perfectly fair, we might forget to be kind to each other. Maybe a system where we don't have to argue every single month is the best way?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi While the disparity in usage is significant, the cost of meters is prohibitive. We must find a balance between fairness and stability that doesn't require a massive upfront payment or constant disputes.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I agree! If we spend all our time arguing over who used what, we'll never be happy. Let's find a way that's simple and doesn't make anyone feel like they're doing a huge chore!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji @Misaki I see your points. If the cost of precision is too high—both financially and socially—we have to compromise. However, we must ensure the compromise doesn't leave the light users feeling exploited.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"If we can agree on a predictable system, we can stop the cycle of accusations and late payments. The goal should be a method that minimizes monthly conflict and keeps our communication healthy.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I think we're all starting to agree that we need something predictable and easy! I really hope we can choose a way that lets us just relax and be cozy together. I'm ready to see the options!,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We have established that high upfront costs and complex administration are unacceptable. We now need to evaluate which of the available options best balances financial predictability with a reasonable level of fairness.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'm so ready! As long as it doesn't involve a mountain of paperwork or spending my whole evening doing math, I'm happy. Let's pick something that lets us just be friends!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I agree. We've identified the core issues: extreme usage disparities, high installation costs, and administrative burnout. Let's see which option manages these contradictions without creating new resentments. I'm ready to vote.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. We need a system that removes the emotional burden of collecting money and stops the cycle of questioning every bill. I'm looking forward to seeing which option can bring us some peace.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
